hnologies, as a tool to evaluate skin lesions prior to determining the need for a biopsy. Their objective is to obtain information in order to validate this skin scanner in the context of its ability to accurately identify basal cell carcinoma skin lesions."},"conditionsModule":{"conditions":["Carcinoma, Basal Cell"],"keywords":["Detection"]},"designModule":{"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","phases":["NA"],"designInfo":{"allocation":"NA","interventionModel":"SINGLE_GROUP","primaryPurpose":"DIAGNOSTIC","maskingInfo":{"masking":"NONE"}},"enrollmentInfo":{"count":60,"type":"ACTUAL"}},"armsInterventionsModule":{"armGroups":[{"label":"WR-22 model microwave sensor","type":"EXPERIMENTAL","interventionNames":["Device: WR-22 model microwave sensor"]}],"interventions":[{"type":"DEVICE","name":"WR-22 model microwave sensor","armGroupLabels":["WR-22 model microwave sensor"]}]},"outcomesModule":{"primaryOutcomes":[{"measure":"Positive predictive value","timeFrame":"Immediately pre-biopsy"}]},"eligibilityModule":{"eligibilityCriteria":"Inclusion Criteria:

